## Pipeline Architecture

```
Every 0.5 s (2 fps):
  read frame
    └── brightness < 60? → skip frame, sleep 30 s (dark-frame guard)
  YOLOv11 (detector.py)
    └── motorcycle bboxes + confidence
    └── license_plate bboxes
  ByteTrack (detector.py)
    └── assigns persistent track_id across frames
  PaddleOCR (detector.py)
    └── reads Thai plate text from plate crop (conf ≥ 0.6)
  K-Means HSV (detector.py)
    └── extracts dominant color from motorcycle crop
  Homography (main.py)
    └── pixel centroid → GPS (lat, lng)
  plate_cache lookup (main.py)
    └── GET /internal/vehicle-by-plate/{plate} → { vehicle_id, geofence_radius_m, color }
  Color-verification gate (main.py)
    └── detected color group ≠ registered color group → suppress all events
  StationaryTracker (tracker.py)
    └── per track_id state machine → event (PARKED | HEARTBEAT | MOVED | None)
  LOST detection (main.py)
    └── track_id disappears from frame while state == "parked" → POST /internal/alert LOST
  Backend internal API calls (main.py)
    └── PARKED    → POST /internal/parked
    └── HEARTBEAT → POST /internal/heartbeat
    └── MOVED     → POST /internal/alert { alert_type: "MOVED" }
    └── LOST      → POST /internal/alert { alert_type: "LOST" }
```

## Current AI Worker Patterns

| Module | Pattern |
|---|---|
| `detector.py` | `detect_and_track(frame)` returns list of dicts with `track_id`, `centroid`, `confidence`, `plate_text`, `detected_color` |
| `detector.py` | ByteTrack initialized with `track_thresh=0.25`, `track_buffer=30`, `match_thresh=0.8` |
| `detector.py` | PaddleOCR `lang="th"`, `use_gpu=True`; accepts confidence ≥ 0.6 only |
| `detector.py` | K-Means with k=3 on 32×32 resized HSV crop; dominant cluster by bincount |
| `tracker.py` | `StationaryTracker.update(track_id, plate, lat, lng)` returns `(event, extra)` |
| `tracker.py` | `STILL_THRESHOLD_DEG = 0.00005` (~5 m at E1 parking lot) |
| `tracker.py` | `HEARTBEAT_SEC = 600` (10 minutes) |
| `tracker.py` | `threshold_minutes` default 2.0 — maps to `users.detection_threshold_min` |
| `main.py` | `plate_cache` dict — prevents repeated `/internal/vehicle-by-plate` calls per session |
| `main.py` | `COLOR_GROUPS` dict — maps color names to groups for verification gate |
| `main.py` | `PIXEL_PTS` / `GPS_PTS` — 4-point homography; must be measured on-site at E1 |
| `main.py` | RTSP reconnect: `cap = cv2.VideoCapture(source)` on frame drop |
| `main.py` | Dev mode: `VIDEO_SOURCE=test_footage.mp4` in `.env` instead of RTSP |

## Internal API Contract

All calls require `X-Secret: $INTERNAL_SECRET` header. Payload must match exactly.

| Event | Endpoint | Required payload fields |
|---|---|---|
| Look up vehicle | `GET /internal/vehicle-by-plate/{plate}` | — → `{ vehicle_id, geofence_radius_m, color }` |
| PARKED | `POST /internal/parked` | `vehicle_id, camera_id, track_id, confidence_score, lat, lng, detection_duration_min` |
| HEARTBEAT | `POST /internal/heartbeat` | same as PARKED + `movement_delta` |
| MOVED | `POST /internal/alert` | same as PARKED + `alert_type: "MOVED"`, `snapshot_url?` |
| LOST | `POST /internal/alert` | same as PARKED + `alert_type: "LOST"`, `snapshot_url?` |

`detection_duration_min` = `(now - still_since) / 60` rounded to 2 decimal places.
`movement_delta` = degree-unit distance `((lat-prev_lat)^2 + (lng-prev_lng)^2)^0.5`.

## Responsibilities

- implement detection, tracking, OCR, and color extraction changes within scope
- maintain stationary state machine correctness: PARKED → HEARTBEAT → MOVED/LOST transitions
- preserve dark-frame guard and RTSP reconnect logic at all times
- preserve color-verification gate — never fire alerts on color mismatch
- preserve `plate_cache` to avoid redundant backend lookups
- update `PIXEL_PTS` / `GPS_PTS` only after on-site E1 measurement — never guess GPS coordinates
- validate internal API payload shape before any backend change that affects `/internal/*`
- test exclusively against a recorded `.mp4` before touching live RTSP
- document model file name (`yolov11s_mfu.pt`) if changed
- produce T13/T15/T16 AI Worker sections for T1-T20 handoff
- identify PRD updates for threshold, pipeline, or state machine changes

## COLOR_GROUPS Reference

Current color-group mapping (in `main.py`):

| Detected color | Group |
|---|---|
| black, charcoal | dark |
| white, silver, grey, gray | light |
| red, maroon, orange | red |
| blue, navy, teal | blue |
| green | green |
| yellow | yellow |

Any change to `vehicles.color` allowed values in MongoDB must be reconciled with this table. If a new color is added to the vehicle schema, add it to the appropriate group or create a new group — and update this PRD table.

## Writing Conditions

- Do not change `STILL_THRESHOLD_DEG` or `HEARTBEAT_SEC` without explicit FR and QA approval — they directly determine when FCM alerts fire.
- Do not remove the dark-frame guard (`mean brightness < 60 → sleep 30 s`).
- Do not remove the RTSP reconnect loop — live camera feed drops require it.
- Do not clear `plate_cache` within a session unless a vehicle lookup returns 404 (plate unregistered).
- Do not fire PARKED/HEARTBEAT/MOVED/LOST events for vehicles whose detected color group ≠ registered color group.
- Do not hardcode GPS coordinates for `PIXEL_PTS` / `GPS_PTS` without real on-site calibration at E1 — placeholder values in the design doc are for development only.
- `track_id` from ByteTrack is an integer; convert to `str(track_id)` before sending in API payload.
- LOST detection must only fire when a `track_id` with `state == "parked"` disappears from the current frame's tracked set — do not fire for vehicles that were never confirmed parked.
- Run offline with `VIDEO_SOURCE=test_footage.mp4` and verify MongoDB documents before connecting to live RTSP.

## Verification Procedure

```bash
# 1. Start backend first
cd backend && uvicorn main:app --reload

# 2. Run AI Worker with test video
cd ai_worker
VIDEO_SOURCE=test_footage.mp4 python main.py

# Expected outputs to verify:
# - tracking_logs documents inserted in MongoDB on PARKED/HEARTBEAT
# - alert_history document inserted on MOVED/LOST
# - route_history document bundled from tracking_logs on MOVED/LOST
# - vehicles.last_location updated with { lat, lng }
# - FCM notification delivered (check Firebase console or device)
```

